cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Foundation: Open standards for socially-beneficial software"
message: "If you use any specification published by The Foundation in academic work, please cite it as below. For project-specific citations, use the version tag prefix corresponding to that project (e.g. ocas-v0.1.0)."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Foundation"
    website: "https://github.com/the-foundation-stack"
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-foundation-stack/Foundation"
abstract: >-
  The Foundation publishes open standards, protocols, reference
  implementations, and research for socially-beneficial software.
  Its first project, the Open Charity API Standard (OCAS), is a
  vendor-neutral OpenAPI 3.1 specification for charity donation APIs,
  with first-class support for international tax-relief schemes and
  faith-based giving categories including Zakat (with the 8 canonical
  Asnaf categories), Sadaqah, Waqf, Qurbani, Aqiqah, Fidya, Kaffarah,
  and interest purification.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
